    "title": "Kids Fishing Derby on Lake Hayward June 6 - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Terrell Boettcher ,\n22 hours ago A Kids Fishing Derby will be held from 9 a.m. to noon Saturday June 6 at Lake Hayward Beach and Park. Registration begins at 8:30 a.m.\nYouths age 1 to 15 will fish from shore around the park and from the large fishing dock. There also will be a casting contest, and a lure-making booth with Frank Pratt. Kids can design and make their own fishing baits.\nPrizes will be awarded to youth for the largest fish in each age category. Bait will be provided and fishing gear will be available to borrow if needed.\nAfter fishing, all participants will earn prizes and receive fishing gear.\nThe Derby is a more than 65-year Hayward tradition. It is sponsored by the Hayward Rod and Gun Club in partnership with Muskies Inc., Sawyer County Outdoor Projects and Education (SCOPE), the Hayward Bass Club, Hayward Bait and Bottle Shop, the Wisconsin DNR, WRLS Radio and several others.",
